{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head `8000f1be71dadaaf88780c85ccf90c998bf4d4c5`, on main `4f9f49a5`.\n\n**The decisions.** I would keep all three scripts.\n\n- `owned-scopes-browser.mjs`: nothing else follows two rooms and the back path, and the repair is small.\n- `screens.mjs`: the width, target-size and keyboard checks earn their place, and the job costs 6 minutes 49 seconds on a page change, outside the gate.\n- `demo-captures.ts`: `docs/demo.md` depends on its deployment form.\n\n**The removed screenshots.** Outside `notes/`, no tracked file names `test/screenshots`, and `check-doc-links` finds 0 broken links at this head.\n\n**\"Fails unattended and unnamed\".** I read `grow-routing-browser.mjs` as you do. It runs by hand, so it does not fail unattended. `docs/testing.md` names its line and its cause, and `76a1c020` owns the repair. I accounted for every browser script in the tree. Each is in a workflow or in the hand-run table, with what it needs, and the Counter's script runs in the gate. The four scripts that need a local Worker did not run for this head, and they cannot run unattended, so the done-when does not reach them. The note says so.\n\n**`recorder-output.ts`.** I found no path that prints the record.\n\n- `recorderLog` builds a new `Error`, so the child-process error and its stdout go no further.\n- The child's stderr still reaches the parent. The recorders print the record by `console.log`, which is stdout, so that does not carry it.\n- `recordFrom`'s messages name only counts, the record's name and the digest's result, and the `JSON.parse` failure is caught and replaced. The Node tests use a marked secret to hold this.\n- Neither workflow uploads an artifact, so no `checks.json` or capture leaves the runner.\n- `22-linux-demo-recorder-prefix.log` matched my search for record lines. It is 572 bytes of analysis, and it quotes the text before a marker and no record.\n- `PAGE_CAPTURE_RECORD_OUT` still writes the record to a file when a person sets it. That is older code, and the workflow does not set it.\n\n**Exit 2.** Nothing in `scripts/`, `package.json` or the other workflows runs `demo-captures.ts`, so the change from exit 0 harms no caller, and a missing tool can no longer pass as a skip.\n\n**Workflows.** `page-browser.yml` holds `contents: read`, pins its actions to the same commits as the card workflow, installs with `--ignore-scripts` in a scratch directory, and checks the integrity of `playwright-core` and the Chromium revision. It uses no secret.\n\n**Evidence and runs.** `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-browser-scripts/` verifies against `SHA256SUMS` `9b8e6d84…` and holds no writable file. The gate exits 0 at `2f2fadd1`. `gh` shows run 41346896436 (card) and run 41346896550 (page) succeeded at `2f2fadd1`, and run 41349477199 (card) succeeded at this head, which meets the rule in `0998f9ec`. The page workflow did not run at this head, because the merge touches none of its paths. `a4008516` is the tree of source commit `c3e6c6e8`, as the note says.\n\nNo gate ran at this head, and I do not ask for one. The merge brings the card's press and J5's note, and it shares no path with this head. At this head I ran `recorder-output.test.mjs` (7 passed) and the seal test (10 passed). `check-notes` and `check-commit-messages` pass, and the worktree is clean.\n\n**Next edit, not blocking.** The note says \"a change that breaks one fails a run at that commit\". That holds for a change on a workflow's path list. Neither list names `packages/scope`, `packages/cli` or `packages/client`, and the recorders run on all of them, so a change only there can still break a script with no run, and the gate skips the recorders. A generated page bundle under `apps/room/page` catches part of that, and `docs/testing.md` states the paths correctly. The cause that broke `screens.mjs` this time, `4f7c1455`, does touch listed paths, so this workflow would have caught it. The planner may want a scheduled run if this drift returns.\n\n**Architecture.** A browser script is now either in a workflow or named with what it needs. The recorder's format gains a line count and a digest, so a lost chunk stops by name. `screens.mjs` writes no tracked file.\n\n**Security.** No product source changes, and the record stays in memory and out of messages. The fixture keys are test keys. The new workflow adds no authority.\n\n**Simplification.** `recorder-output.ts` replaces two copies of the same parsing, and the head removes 3,555 lines, mostly tracked outputs that no test read.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ec9135f308d08eeaaa75eb899a4e936be6bd1ca4","binding":"assigned","head":"8000f1be71dadaaf88780c85ccf90c998bf4d4c5","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4e00874e93d41cd499187541e4f51f896046f570\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d9b909a57fffbd3a4d20ee77407df601ff0a1065\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1be847a1f9d774a851f5ec0fdcdb0e0420fb7e15","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}